        <h2>A move for your parent, <em>without you taking on everything</em></h2>
        <p class="rx-sub">When a parent needs to move, the job often falls to adult children who are already busy and may live hours away. Chayce coordinates the practical side so your parent stays at the centre.</p>
        <ul class="rx-points"><li><i class="fas fa-user-friends" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>One point of contact</h3><p>A coordinator who plans the move with you, keeps everyone updated and handles the day itself.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-box-open" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Sorting and packing</h3><p>We help sort and pack their belongings, and stage the current home for sale.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-file-signature" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Agents and solicitors</h3><p>We liaise with estate agents and solicitors and arrange a fully insured removal.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-home" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Settled from day one</h3><p>We unpack and set up the new home so it feels familiar from the first evening.</p></li></ul>
        <p class="rx-where">We start with a <a href="/discovery/">Discovery Consultation</a>, from &pound;{{ (site.packages | findByKey("discovery")).price | gbp }}, by phone or in person, which can include you and your parent together. It produces a written plan, timeline and budget, so the whole family knows what will happen and when. Whether the move is to a smaller home, closer to family, into a retirement village or somewhere with more support, the approach is the same.</p>
